  "summary": "A technique creating images by scratching through a dark surface layer to reveal a lighter substrate beneath.",
  "description": "Involves layering a dark, often inked surface over a lighter board, then using sharp tools to scratch through the dark layer to create white lines and textures. Developed as an alternative to wood engraving, later adopted by illustrators and contemporary artists for its dramatic contrast and graphic quality.",
